# Routh II.Arts.180-183 — motion when A = B: steady precession with two
# different periods — dynamic notebook
#
# E. J. Routh, "The Advanced Part of a Treatise on the Dynamics of a System of
# Rigid Bodies", Part II (Macmillan, 6th ed. 1905), Arts. 180-183, "Motion when
# A = B". When two principal moments are equal the general elliptic-function
# solution of Art. 139 degenerates into circular functions and everything is
# elementary: the polhodes become CIRCLES about the figure axis, and the motion
# is a steady precession.
#
# TWO PERIODS, NOT ONE. This is what makes the case worth watching. There are
# two distinct circular motions going on at once, at different rates:
#
#   IN SPACE   the figure axis sweeps a cone about the invariable line at the
#              precession rate      psi-dot = G / A
#
#   IN THE BODY the instantaneous axis sweeps a cone about the figure axis at
#              the rate            (A - C) w3 / A
#
# Neither rate is the other, and neither is |w|. A body doing this looks like it
# has one motion; it has two, and they are incommensurable in general.
#
# THE NUMBERS. A cuboid of mass 3 with half-extents (1, 1, 2) has
#
#     I = diag(5, 5, 2)      so   A = B = 5,  C = 2,  figure axis z
#
# Started at w = (0.6, 0, 3):
#
#     L = (3, 0, 6)                        G = |L| = 6.708203932499369
#     precession in space  G/A            = 1.3416407864998738
#         period 2*pi/(G/A)               = 4.6832098206938175
#     body-frame rate (A-C)w3/A           = 1.8
#         period 2*pi/1.8                 = 3.490658503988659
#
# THE TEST. After exactly 2*pi/1.8 the body-frame angular velocity must return
# to its starting value (0.6, 0, 3) -- one turn of the body cone. Two further
# invariants are printed throughout: |w| is CONSTANT here, unlike the
# asymmetric case, and so is the angle between w and L. Both are consequences
# of A = B and both fail the moment the symmetry is broken.
#
# SETUP NOTE. system.g_constant = 0 so nothing else acts.
#
# WHAT YOU WATCH: a square-section box in a smooth, steady wobble -- the
# textbook picture of precession, with none of the irregularity of the
# asymmetric case.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LAUNCH (run from the repository root: /Users/nsh/Developer/code/rust/rustSimulate)
#
#     posim_notebook routh_p2_uniaxal_precession
#
# or, without the shell alias, the always-available form:
#
#     cargo run -p posim --release -- --notebook dynamic_notebooks/routh_p2_uniaxal_precession.posim
#
# The scene window opens in your browser. To start the simulation, press Start
# in that window, or type this at the In[] prompt in the terminal:
#
#     scene start
#
# If no browser should be launched (the URL is printed instead), use:
#
#     POSIM_NO_BROWSER=1 cargo run -p posim --release -- --notebook dynamic_notebooks/routh_p2_uniaxal_precession.posim
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

set system.g_constant = 0
set system.rtol = 1e-13
set system.atol = 1e-15

new cuboid { mass = 3, half_extents = [1, 1, 2], angular_velocity = [0.6, 0, 3] }

get obj0.inertia_tensor
get obj0.angular_momentum
norm(obj0.angular_momentum)
# |w| and the cone angle -- both constant for a uniaxal body
norm(obj0.angular_velocity)
dot(obj0.angular_velocity, obj0.angular_momentum) / (norm(obj0.angular_velocity) * norm(obj0.angular_momentum))

# one turn of the BODY cone: 2*pi/1.8 = 3.490658503988659
run 3.490658503988659 steps 4
[obj0.orientation.w, 0 - obj0.orientation.x, 0 - obj0.orientation.y, 0 - obj0.orientation.z] * [0, obj0.angular_velocity.x, obj0.angular_velocity.y, obj0.angular_velocity.z] * obj0.orientation
norm(obj0.angular_velocity)
dot(obj0.angular_velocity, obj0.angular_momentum) / (norm(obj0.angular_velocity) * norm(obj0.angular_momentum))

# a second turn -- still exact
run 3.490658503988659 steps 4
[obj0.orientation.w, 0 - obj0.orientation.x, 0 - obj0.orientation.y, 0 - obj0.orientation.z] * [0, obj0.angular_velocity.x, obj0.angular_velocity.y, obj0.angular_velocity.z] * obj0.orientation
norm(obj0.angular_velocity)
reset

set system.g_constant = 0
set system.rtol = 1e-13
set system.atol = 1e-15
new cuboid { mass = 3, half_extents = [1, 1, 2], angular_velocity = [0.6, 0, 3] }

scene create
scene set_time_step 0.02
